  "Number": 9,
  "Question": "A function \\(f\\) has the property that \\(f(3x-1)=x^2+x+1\\) for all real numbers \\(x.\\) What is \\(f(5)?\\)",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(7\\)",
    "B": "\\(13\\)",
    "C": "\\(31\\)",
    "D": "\\(111\\)",
    "E": "\\(211\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "To obtain \\(f(5)\\) from the given identity, choose \\(x\\) so that \\(3x-1=5\\). Solving gives \\(x=2\\), which is allowed because the identity holds for every real \\(x\\). Substituting yields\n\\[\nf(5)=f(3\\cdot2-1)=2^2+2+1=7.\n\\]\nThus \\(\\boxed{f(5)=7}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{A}}\\).",
